    {
      "id": "authentication:d7153d263a6a",
      "content_hash": "d7153d263a6a",
      "title": "Verify DB-aligned final state after return/cancel updates",
      "lesson": "When submitting cancellations/returns/refunds via tools and then concluding the authentication workflow. | No explicit end-to-end verification that the persisted order state (order IDs, exact return_items set, refund method IDs, and resulting status/required fields) matched what the evaluator/DB check expects. | After tool submission, re-fetch the affected order(s) (and/or any available validation endpoint) and cross-check: order status, returned item IDs list, refund/payment method ID, and totals/fields required by the system; only then provide the final confirmation to the user.",
      "applicability": "When submitting cancellations/returns/refunds via tools and then concluding the authentication workflow.",
      "family": "authentication",
      "outcome_type": "failure",
      "retrieval_text": "Title: Verify DB-aligned final state after return/cancel updates\nApplicability: When submitting cancellations/returns/refunds via tools and then concluding the authentication workflow.\nLesson: When submitting cancellations/returns/refunds via tools and then concluding the authentication workflow. | No explicit end-to-end verification that the persisted order state (order IDs, exact return_items set, refund method IDs, and resulting status/required fields) matched what the evaluator/DB check expects. | After tool submission, re-fetch the affected order(s) (and/or any available validation endpoint) and cross-check: order status, returned item IDs list, refund/payment method ID, and totals/fields required by the system; only then provide the final confirmation to the user.\nFamily: authentication\nOutcome: failure",
